  "limitations_md": "\n### Intended use\nResearch prototype for single 2D brain MRI slices (mostly T1 contrast-enhanced, BRISC-like). **Not a medical device; not for diagnosis.**\n### How to read the output\n* **Answered** - every safety check passed: the calibrated confidence is above the threshold that *proves* >= 95 % accuracy on validation\n  images, the image is similar to the training data, classification and segmentation agree, and the head was found.\n* **Referred** - one of the checks failed. This is the intended behaviour for uncertain, unusual or colour images, not a malfunction.\n* The attention map shows where the classifier pooled its evidence; it is not a diagnosis and not a segmentation.\n### Known limitations\n* One slice at a time; no 3D context, no other MRI sequences, no patient history.\n* Trained on public datasets without reliable patient IDs (near-duplicate groups were used instead); retrospective data only.\n* Accuracy on images from new hospitals, scanners or the web can be lower; that is why the app refers images it is not sure about.\n* Dice on the TCGA-LGG set is approximate (FLAIR masks).\n"
